.TH cksum 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
cksum \- compute and verify file checksums
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY cksum
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.RI [ FILE \~.\|.\|.\&]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Print or verify checksums.
By default use the 32 bit CRC algorithm.
.PP
With no FILE, or when FILE is \-, read standard input.
.PP
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum\-a
\fB\-a, \-\-algorithm=\,TYPE\fP
.UE
select the digest type to use.  See DIGEST below
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum\-\-base64
\fB\-\-base64\fP
.UE
emit base64\-encoded digests, not hexadecimal
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum\-c
\fB\-c, \-\-check\fP
.UE
read checksums from the FILEs and check them
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum\-l
\fB\-l, \-\-length=\,BITS\fP
.UE
digest length in bits; must not exceed the max size
and must be a multiple of 8 for blake2b;
must be 224, 256, 384, or 512 for sha2 or sha3
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum\-\-raw
\fB\-\-raw\fP
.UE
emit a raw binary digest, not hexadecimal
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum\-\-tag
\fB\-\-tag\fP
.UE
create a BSD\-style checksum (the default)
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum\-\-untagged
\fB\-\-untagged\fP
.UE
create a reversed style checksum, without digest type
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum\-z
\fB\-z, \-\-zero\fP
.UE
end each output line with NUL, not newline,
and disable file name escaping
.SS "The following five options are useful only when verifying checksums:"
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum\-\-ignore\-missing
\fB\-\-ignore\-missing\fP
.UE
don't fail or report status for missing files
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum\-\-quiet
\fB\-\-quiet\fP
.UE
don't print OK for each successfully verified file
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum\-\-status
\fB\-\-status\fP
.UE
don't output anything, status code shows success
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum\-\-strict
\fB\-\-strict\fP
.UE
exit non\-zero for improperly formatted checksum lines
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum\-w
\fB\-w, \-\-warn\fP
.UE
warn about improperly formatted checksum lines
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cksum\-\-debug
\fB\-\-debug\fP
.UE
indicate which implementation used
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/cksum#cksum\-\-help
\fB\-\-help\fP
.UE
display this help and exit
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/cksum#cksum\-\-version
\fB\-\-version\fP
.UE
output version information and exit
.SS "DIGEST determines the digest algorithm and default output format:"
.TP
sysv
(equivalent to sum \fB\-s\fR)
.TP
bsd
(equivalent to sum \fB\-r\fR)
.TP
crc
(equivalent to cksum)
.TP
crc32b
(only available through cksum)
.TP
md5
(equivalent to md5sum)
.TP
sha1
(equivalent to sha1sum)
.TP
sha2
(equivalent to sha{224,256,384,512}sum)
.TP
sha3
(only available through cksum)
.TP
blake2b
(equivalent to b2sum)
.TP
sm3
(only available through cksum)
.PP
When checking, the input should be a former output of this program,
or equivalent standalone program.
